From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:27:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/34] surface_lazy: name the refused takes, scope them, and
 leave a displayed surface's writes ahead

Under surface_lazy, every remap and every replaceRegion of any texture moved
one global epoch, which refused every surface's next take. stderr now counts
takes by reason and copies in by cause, per surface too.

New live switches, default off, nothing changes without them:
- surface_lazy_scoped: a remap or CPU write drops the standing of the
  surfaces over those pages alone.
- surface_lazy_present: a surface the display presented leaves its writes
  ahead in its image; a present, a command buffer using its bytes, a CPU call
  through a texture or a clock copies them back, once, in a command buffer of
  its own, inside the union of the scissors.
- surface_lazy_present_all: every lazy surface.
- surface_lazy_present_max_ms: the clock's bound (default 100).
- surface_lazy_min_width: keeps narrower surfaces out (default none).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
